  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ムラサキムカシヨモギ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%A0%E3%83%A9%E3%82%B5%E3%82%AD%E3%83%A0%E3%82%AB%E3%82%B7%E3%83%A8%E3%83%A2%E3%82%AE",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 107023976,
      "text": "ムラサキムカシヨモギ Cyanthillium cinereum は、キク科の草本。ひょろひょろと伸び、紫色のヤグルマギクを小さくしたような花を付ける。別名にヤンバルヒゴタイがある。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Cyanthillium cinereum」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyanthillium_cinereum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1371114072,
      "text": "Cyanthillium cinereum is a species of perennial plants in the sunflower family. The species is native to tropical Africa and to tropical Asia and has become naturalized in Australia, Mesoamerica, tropical South America, the West Indies, and the US State of Florida."
    }
  },
